mdl 1;
-- Bug mendixlabs/mxcli#1549 (ako/mxcli#1447): Web UI settings (OptimizedClient)
-- cannot be described or altered
--
-- Symptom:
--   $ mxcli -p App.mpr -c "list settings"
--   | Web UI Settings         | OptimizedClient: Yes |
--   $ mxcli -p App.mpr -c "describe settings"          -- no Web UI section
--   $ mxcli exec webui.mdl -p App.mpr
--   Error: unknown settings section: webui (expected model, configuration, constant, LANGUAGE, or workflows)
--
-- UseOptimizedClient picks the client the app runs on — Yes the React client, No
-- the classic (Dojo) one, MigrationMode Mendix's mixed mode — and `run --local`
-- and the create-page skill both depend on it, so an agent setting up an app from
-- MDL could not set it, and one reading `describe settings` could not see it.
--
-- Fix: `alter settings webui (OptimizedClient: …)` writes
-- Forms$WebUIProjectSettingsPart.UseOptimizedClient (the backend used to pass that
-- part through as read, so adding only the executor case would have reported
-- "Updated" and written nothing), and DESCRIBE SETTINGS emits it.
--
-- Measured on a blank 11.14.0 app: `mx check` reports 0 errors after
-- `alter settings webui (OptimizedClient: 'No')` wrote the property, and ALSO
-- 0 errors with an out-of-range value ('React') forced into it
-- — so the MDL-SET03 refusal of a non-member is the only thing that catches one.
--
-- Manual verification:
--   mxcli exec 1549-alter-settings-webui.mdl -p app.mpr
--   mxcli -p app.mpr -c "describe settings"   → alter settings webui ( OptimizedClient: 'Yes' );

alter settings webui (OptimizedClient: 'No');

-- Matched case-insensitively, stored in Mendix's spelling.
alter settings webui (OptimizedClient: 'yes');
